Sval: Remove the password manager's save and update prompts

Firefox's password manager is locked off (Sval spec §7.3), so it never
offers to save or update a password. The prompter and its doorhanger go
with the doorhanger's username field component and strings, and so
does the HTTP authentication prompt's step that offered to save what the
user entered. The prompter's component and interface go too, as does
the simple autocomplete search only the doorhanger's username field
used. The address bar keeps the password icon, which Relay anchors to.

